    "body": "### Problem\n\n`textDocument/didSave` notifies every client, including unattached ones.\n\nThis is not the case for things like `textDocument/didChange`, which guards on running and attached:\n\n```lua\n-- runtime/lua/vim/lsp/_changetracking.lua:324\nfor _, client in pairs(state.clients) do\n  if not client:is_stopped() and vim.lsp.buf_is_attached(bufnr, client.id) then\n```\n\n### Steps to reproduce\n\n`nvim --clean -u` this lua file:\n\n```lua\nlocal log = {}\n\n-- fake lsp\nlocal function fake(name)\n\treturn function()\n\t\tlocal closing = false\n\t\treturn {\n\t\t\trequest = function(method, _, callback)\n\t\t\t\tif method == \"initialize\" then\n\t\t\t\t\tcallback(nil, {\n\t\t\t\t\t\tcapabilities = {\n\t\t\t\t\t\t\ttextDocumentSync = { openClose = true, change = 2, save = true },\n\t\t\t\t\t\t},\n\t\t\t\t\t})\n\t\t\t\telseif method == \"shutdown\" then\n\t\t\t\t\tcallback(nil, nil)\n\t\t\t\tend\n\t\t\t\treturn true, 1\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t\tnotify = function(method, params)\n\t\t\t\tlocal uri = params and params.textDocument and params.textDocument.uri or \"\"\n\t\t\t\tlog[#log + 1] = (\"%s  <-  %s  %s\"):format(name, method, vim.fn.fnamemodify(uri, \":t\"))\n\t\t\t\treturn true\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t\tis_closing = function()\n\t\t\t\treturn closing\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t\tterminate = function()\n\t\t\t\tclosing = true\n\t\t\tend,\n\t\t}\n\tend\nend\n\nvim.cmd.edit(\"a\")\nvim.lsp.start({ name = \"server_a\", cmd = fake(\"server_a\") })\n\nvim.cmd.edit(\"b\")\nvim.lsp.start({ name = \"server_b\", cmd = fake(\"server_b\") })\n\nvim.cmd.write()\nvim.wait(200)\n\nfor _, line in ipairs(log) do\n\tprint(line)\nend\n```\n\n### Expected behavior\n\nIn repro, `server_a` shouldn't receive anything about file `b`.\n\n### Nvim version (nvim -v)\n\n0.13.0-dev-1183+g7b28b1f4a9\n\n### Vim (not Nvim) behaves the same?\n\nno\n\n### Operating system/version\n\n7.2.0-rc5-1-MANJARO\n\n### Terminal name/version\n\nkitty 0.48.1\n\n### $TERM environment variable\n\nxterm-kitty\n\n### Installation\n\nAUR",
